// A non-void function that falls off the end must be rejected — BY KAMA, with a kama-level message.
// It used to be caught only by clang (-Werror=return-type), so the error named generated C and
// `kama check` — the path the language server runs — reported the file clean. That was the last
// disagreement between `kama check` and `kama build`; see CEmitter::alwaysExits, and
// tests/return_paths.kama for the shapes that must still be ACCEPTED.
fn int32 compute(int32 a) { int32 y = a + 1; }
fn int main() { return compute(a: 41); }
